-- title:
--   Places extend along separable constant field extensions
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $K'$, $F$, $F'$ be fields fitting into compatible towers $K \subseteq K' \subseteq F'$ and $K \subseteq F \subseteq F'$ (the scalar actions being related by the usual tower conditions). Assume $K'/K$ is algebraic and separable, $F'/F$ is integral, the $F$-subalgebra of $F'$ generated by the image of $K'$ is all of $F'$, and $K$ is algebraically closed in $F$ in the sense that every $y \in F$ algebraic over $K$ lies in the image of $K$. Let $M$ be a further field with $F \subseteq M \subseteq F'$ compatibly over $K$, with $F'/M$ integral, and let $V$ be a place of $M$ over $K$, i.e. a valuation subring $\mathcal{O}_V \subseteq M$ containing the image of $K$, different from $M$ itself, and a principal ideal ring. Then there exists a place $W$ of $F'$ over $K'$, i.e. a valuation subring $\mathcal{O}_W \subseteq F'$ containing the image of $K'$, proper and a principal ideal ring, whose contraction along $M \to F'$ is exactly $\mathcal{O}_V$; here $W$ is first regarded as a place of $F'$ over $K$ by keeping the same valuation subring.
--
--   This is the extension theorem for places in a separable constant field extension $F' = FK'$: restriction of places from $F'/K'$ to any intermediate layer $M$ (in particular to $F$ itself, taking $M = F$) is surjective, the extension $F'/M$ being allowed to be infinite. It underlies the fibre-counting and degree identities for constant field extensions, such as the comparison of the degree of a place with the cardinality of its fibre, the pullback of divisors along constant field extensions, and the invariance of the genus under constant field extension.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_exists_forgetConstants_restrict_eq_of_isConstantFieldExtension.lean

